Respond with ONLY a JSON object that validates against the following schema.
No prose, no code fences, no explanation.

<json_schema>
{
  "description": "LLM response: a value for each hole, keyed by parameter name.",
  "properties": {
    "values": {
      "additionalProperties": {
        "type": "string"
      },
      "title": "Values",
      "type": "object"
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "values"
  ],
  "title": "Bindings",
  "type": "object"
}
</json_schema>

[system]
You fill typed data holes in a reusable plan for a new task. Change only the data — never the leading program, directory, or host. Return a value for every hole.

[user]
Task: x

Holes to fill (keep each head `/work` exactly):
- p: fills the `postcondition` of a step whose head is `/work`; past values: ['/work/out.txt']

Return {name: concrete value} for every hole.

